    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a challenging slate today, with our two active starters operating in the marginal-to-strong transition zone. **Junior Caminero** earns the highest designation of the day at 51.25, buoyed by a prime #3 hole placement and a favorable platoon look against Misiorowski. While Misiorowski\u2019s sub-3.00 xERA remains a significant hurdle that drags down his raw expectation, **Junior Caminero**\u2019s recent form and situational utility keep him in the lineup despite the elite arm. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** sits just behind him at 50.66; while Rasmussen is a respectable arm, the platoon advantage is the primary driver here, as **Christian Yelich** continues to be a stabilizer for our core production metrics. \n\nGiven that the rest of our roster\u2014including **Yordan Alvarez**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Trea Turner**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, **Colt Keith**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Carson Benge**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez**\u2014is sidelined due to scheduled off-days, our bench management is effectively moot today. There are no difficult start/sit dilemmas, as the schedule has stripped us of our speed threats like **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Caleb Durbin**, as well as the power-heavy bat of **Yordan Alvarez**. We are essentially forced into a \"survival mode\" lineup, relying on the discipline of **Junior Caminero** and the veteran eye of **Christian Yelich** to navigate tough matchups while keeping our game caps protected for later in the week.",
